---
import { version } from '../../../../../package.json';

const cdnSnippet = `<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/aster-ds@${version}/dist/css/aster.css">
<script type="module">
  import { initAsterComponents } from 'https://unpkg.com/aster-ds@${version}/dist/js/aster.js';
  initAsterComponents();
</script>`;
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

const npmInstallSnippet = `npm install aster-ds`;

const pmInstallSnippet = `# pnpm
pnpm add aster-ds

# yarn
yarn add aster-ds`;

const cssImportSnippet = `// All-in-one stylesheet (tokens + components)
import 'aster-ds/aster.css';`;

const cssIndivSnippet = `import 'aster-ds/tokens.css';
import 'aster-ds/components.css';`;

const jsInitSnippet = `import { initAsterComponents } from 'aster-ds';

// Initialize interactive behaviors across the document tree
initAsterComponents(document);`;

const fontSnippet = `<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bebas+Neue&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Merriweather:ital,wght@0,300;0,400;0,700;1,300&family=Space+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">`;
---

<DocsLayout 
  title="Installation — Aster Design System"
  description="How to install and configure Aster DS in modern web applications."
  currentPath="/docs/installation"
>
  <article class="doc-view" id="view-installation" data-title="Installation" data-section="docs" aria-labelledby="t-installation">
    <header class="page-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Getting Started</div>
      <h1 id="t-installation" tabindex="-1">Installation</h1>
      <p class="lead">Install, import, and configure Aster DS in modern web applications using npm or direct browser distributions.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="doc-body">
      <section class="doc-section">
        <h2>Before you start</h2>
        <p>Aster is plain HTML, CSS, and browser JavaScript, so no framework is required. You need npm, pnpm, or yarn for a package install, or nothing at all for the CDN option below. It targets current browsers because it relies on modern CSS, such as <code>color-mix()</code> and <code>:has()</code>.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- 1. Package Installation -->
      <section class="doc-section">
        <h2>1. Install using npm</h2>
        <p>Install the official Aster DS package from the npm registry:</p>
        <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
          <div class="code-block__bar">
            <div class="code-block__meta"><span>Terminal</span></div>
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn">Copy Code</button>
          </div>
          <pre><code>{npmInstallSnippet}</code></pre>
        </div>

        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--doc-muted); margin: 0 0 8px;">Or with your preferred package manager:</p>
        <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
          <div class="code-block__bar">
            <div class="code-block__meta"><span>Terminal</span></div>
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn">Copy Code</button>
          </div>
          <pre><code>{pmInstallSnippet}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Import Styles -->
      <section class="doc-section">
        <h2>2. Import CSS Stylesheets</h2>
        <p>Import Aster's compiled stylesheets in your application's entrypoint or layout:</p>
        <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
          <div class="code-block__bar">
            <div class="code-block__meta"><span>JavaScript / CSS Entry</span></div>
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn">Copy Code</button>
          </div>
          <pre><code>{cssImportSnippet}</code></pre>
        </div>

        <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--doc-muted); margin: 0 0 8px;">Or import tokens and components separately:</p>
        <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
          <div class="code-block__bar">
            <div class="code-block__meta"><span>JavaScript / CSS Entry</span></div>
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn">Copy Code</button>
          </div>
          <pre><code>{cssIndivSnippet}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. Typography Setup -->
      <section class="doc-section">
        <h2>3. Typography Web Fonts</h2>
        <p>Include the 4 canonical Google Fonts in your document's <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>:</p>
        <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
          <div class="code-block__bar">
            <div class="code-block__meta"><span>HTML &lt;head&gt;</span></div>
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn">Copy Code</button>
          </div>
          <pre><code>{fontSnippet}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. Interactive Behaviors -->
      <section class="doc-section">
        <h2>4. Initialize Behaviors</h2>
        <p>Aster components feature zero runtime framework dependencies. Initialize delegated behaviors (dialog focus trap, ripple effects, drawer dismiss) once on mount:</p>
        <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
          <div class="code-block__bar">
            <div class="code-block__meta"><span>Client Entry</span></div>
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn">Copy Code</button>
          </div>
          <pre><code>{jsInitSnippet}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

<section class="doc-section">
        <h2>5. Use a CDN instead</h2>
        <p>For a quick prototype with no build step, load Aster directly. Pin the version so updates can't change your page unexpectedly.</p>
        <div class="code-block" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
          <div class="code-block__bar">
            <div class="code-block__meta"><span>HTML</span></div>
            <button type="button" class="copy-btn">Copy Code</button>
          </div>
          <pre><code>{cdnSnippet}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="doc-section">
        <h2>6. Check it works</h2>
        <p>Add a button. If it looks like a dark or white pill and reacts when hovered, the stylesheet is loading.</p>
        <div class="spec-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Troubleshooting">
          <table class="spec-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Problem</th><th scope="col">Likely cause</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Components have no styling</td><td>The stylesheet isn't imported, or only <code>components.css</code> is loaded without <code>tokens.css</code>.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Fonts look wrong</td><td>The web fonts in step 3 aren't loaded.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Dialogs, tabs, or menus don't respond</td><td><code>initAsterComponents()</code> wasn't called.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Dark mode doesn't apply</td><td>Set <code>data-theme="dark"</code> on the <code>html</code> element.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>The Select menu looks plain</td><td>That browser doesn't support <code>appearance: base-select</code>, so it shows its native menu. It still works.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

            <!-- Navigation footer -->
      <nav class="doc-pagination" aria-label="Documentation Pagination" style="margin-top: 48px;">
        <a href="/docs" class="doc-pagination__link doc-pagination__link--prev" rel="prev">
          <span class="doc-pagination__dir"><svg class="as-icon" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow-left"/></svg> Previous</span>
          <span class="doc-pagination__title">&larr; Introduction</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/color" class="doc-pagination__link doc-pagination__link--next" rel="next">
          <span class="doc-pagination__dir">Next <svg class="as-icon" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></span>
          <span class="doc-pagination__title">Color &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
